{"kind":"article","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/astronomykit\/timeandobservers"]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/GettingStarted"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Essentials","title":"Essentials"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Work with astronomical time and geographic observer locations."}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"AstronomyKit"}],"role":"article","title":"Time and Observers"},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/TimeAndObservers","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Accurate time handling is fundamental to astronomy. AstronomyKit provides ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/AstroTime"},{"text":" for precise time representation and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AstronomyKit\/documentation\/AstronomyKit\/Observer"},{"text":" for geographic locations.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Working-with-Time","text":"Working with Time","level":2},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Creating-Times","text":"Creating Times","level":3},{"type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ Current time","let now = AstroTime.now","","\/\/ From calendar components (in UTC)","let eclipse = AstroTime(year: 2024, month: 4, day: 8, hour: 18, minute: 15)","","\/\/ From Foundation Date","let time = AstroTime(Date())","","\/\/ From Julian days since J2000","let jd = AstroTime(ut: 9132.5)"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Time-Arithmetic","text":"Time Arithmetic","level":3},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let now = AstroTime.now","","\/\/ Add days or hours","let tomorrow = now.addingDays(1)","let nextHour = now.addingHours(1)","let lastWeek = now.addingDays(-7)","","\/\/ Compare times","if tomorrow > now {","    print(\"Tomorrow comes after now\")","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Converting-to-Date","text":"Converting to Date","level":3},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let time = AstroTime.now","let date: Date = time.date","","\/\/ Format for display","let formatter = DateFormatter()","formatter.dateStyle = .medium","formatter.timeStyle = .short","print(formatter.string(from: time.date))"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Understanding-UT-vs-TT","text":"Understanding UT vs TT","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"AstroTime stores two time values internally:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Universal Time (UT)"}]},{"text":": Based on Earth’s rotation, used for rise\/set times","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Terrestrial Time (TT)"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Uniform time scale, used for planetary orbits"}]}]}]},{"code":["let time = AstroTime.now","print(\"UT: \\(time.universalTime)\")  \/\/ Days since J2000 noon (UTC)","print(\"TT: \\(time.terrestrialTime)\")  \/\/ Days since J2000 noon (TT)","","\/\/ Create from Terrestrial Time directly","let fromTT = AstroTime(tt: 9132.5)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The difference (ΔT) is automatically handled by AstronomyKit.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Delta T Configuration","anchor":"Delta-T-Configuration","type":"heading","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The difference between TT and UT (called ΔT) varies over time and is estimated"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"using a model. AstronomyKit defaults to the Espenak-Meeus model, but you can"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"switch to JPL Horizons for compatibility:"}]},{"code":["\/\/ Switch to JPL Horizons Delta T model","AstronomyConfig.setDeltaTModel(.jplHorizons)","","\/\/ Query Delta T for a specific time","let deltaT = AstronomyConfig.deltaTEspenakMeeus(universalTime: 0)  \/\/ Seconds at J2000","","\/\/ Reset to defaults","AstronomyConfig.reset()"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"text":"Sidereal Time","anchor":"Sidereal-Time","type":"heading","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Get the sidereal time at the prime meridian:"}]},{"code":["let sidereal = AstroTime.now.siderealTime","print(\"Greenwich Sidereal Time: \\(sidereal) hours\")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Calculate local sidereal time for any longitude:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["let observer = Observer(latitude: 40.7, longitude: -74.0)  \/\/ NYC","let lst = AstroTime.now.siderealTime(longitude: observer.longitude)","print(\"Local Sidereal Time: \\(lst) hours\")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"text":"Working with Observers","anchor":"Working-with-Observers","type":"heading","level":2},{"text":"Creating Observers","anchor":"Creating-Observers","type":"heading","level":3},{"code":["\/\/ Basic location (sea level)","let seattle = Observer(latitude: 47.6062, longitude: -122.3321)","","\/\/ With height above sea level (meters)","let everest = Observer(","    latitude: 27.9881,","    longitude: 86.9250,","    height: 8848.86",")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"text":"Coordinate Conventions","anchor":"Coordinate-Conventions","type":"heading","level":3},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Latitude"}]},{"type":"text","text":": -90° (south) to +90° (north)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Longitude"}]},{"type":"text","text":": -180° (west) to +180° (east)"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Height"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Meters above sea level"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"text":"Built-in Locations","anchor":"Built-in-Locations","type":"heading","level":3},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let greenwich = Observer.greenwich       \/\/ Royal Observatory","let primeMeridian = Observer.primeMeridian  \/\/ 0°, 0°"],"type":"codeListing"},{"text":"Observer Properties","anchor":"Observer-Properties","type":"heading","level":3},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let observer = Observer(latitude: 40.0, longitude: -105.0, height: 1600)","","\/\/ Local gravity (accounts for latitude and altitude)","let gravity = observer.gravity  \/\/ m\/s²","","\/\/ Atmospheric conditions at this elevation","let atmosphere = try observer.atmosphere","print(\"Pressure: \\(atmosphere.pressure) mbar\")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"text":"Observer Vectors","anchor":"Observer-Vectors","type":"heading","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Get the observer’s position relative to Earth’s center:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let observer = Observer.greenwich","","\/\/ Position vector in AU","let position = try observer.vector(at: .now)","","\/\/ Full state (position and velocity)","let state = try observer.state(at: .now)","print(\"Position: \\(state.position)\")","print(\"Velocity: \\(state.velocity)\")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"text":"Time Zones","anchor":"Time-Zones","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"AstronomyKit works entirely in UTC. Convert to local time using Foundation:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let sunrise = try CelestialBody.sun.riseTime(after: .now, from: observer)!","","let formatter = DateFormatter()","formatter.timeZone = TimeZone(identifier: \"America\/New_York\")","formatter.timeStyle = .short","print(\"Sunrise (local): \\(formatter.string(from: sunrise.date))\")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"text":"Codable Support","anchor":"Codable-Support","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Both types support ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for persistence:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let observer = Observer(latitude: 40.7, longitude: -74.0)","let data = try JSONEncoder().encode(observer)","","let time = AstroTime.now","let timeData = try JSONEncoder().encode(time)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"text":"Civil time and numerical compatibility","anchor":"Civil-time-and-numerical-compatibility","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"AstroTime(Date)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", calendar components and ","type":"text"},{"code":".now","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" use civil UTC. From 1961 onward,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a bundled USNO table converts UTC to TT, including the rate adjustments before"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"1972. Future dates retain the last announced leap-second offset. Before 1961,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"civil dates use the engine’s historical UT1 proxy.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"universalTime"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init(ut:)"},{"text":" are modeled UT1 coordinates, not UTC timestamps.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"terrestrialTime"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init(tt:)"},{"text":" are TT. Native search results already carry","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"both scales; their ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".date"},{"text":" uses the same civil inverse as every other time.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"addingDays"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"addingHours"},{"text":" add UT1 coordinate intervals. For civil calendar","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"arithmetic, use Foundation and construct a new ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AstroTime"},{"text":" from the resulting date.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Foundation cannot represent leap seconds. TT instants in positive UTC gaps map"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to the next transition; negative historical steps choose the later civil"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"occurrence. Those instants cannot round-trip through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Date"},{"type":"text","text":". Positive gaps in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"the selected Delta T model similarly map TT to the first UT1 coordinate after","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the jump. At negative overlaps, fixed-point iteration returns the first solution","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reached from its initial ","type":"text"},{"code":"ut = tt","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" estimate. TT remains exact in memory, but","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"numeric Codable remains UT1-based, so decoding a gap-clamped value derives TT","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"again from the selected model. The table’s future convention and the modeled","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"UT1 values do not establish future UTC or Earth-orientation accuracy. Review","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"serialized times and invalidate version-dependent cached calculations when","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"upgrading.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"references":{"doc://AstronomyKit/documentation/AstronomyKit/Observer":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"tex